    <!-- Toolbar icon geometry, one per formatting command (Requirements.md §8). Sourced from Tabler
         Icons (tabler.io/icons, MIT licensed), outline set — each is stroke geometry in a 24x24
         viewBox, not a filled silhouette, so consuming Path elements must set Stroke (not Fill) with
         StrokeThickness="2" and round line caps/joins to render correctly; see the implicit Path
         style in MainWindow.xaml's ToolBar.Resources. Geometry is theme-independent (only the Stroke
         brush changes with theme), so this dictionary is merged once in App.xaml and never swapped
         the way Themes/Light.xaml / Dark.xaml are. -->

    <!-- Editor-mode toggle: swapped in code-behind (MainWindow.UpdateLivePreviewState) between the
         two, showing the icon for the mode a click would switch TO, not the current mode. A closed
         eye for "currently previewing, click to see code" reads more clearly than reusing the
         inline-code "</>" glyph, which is already taken by the Inline Code button elsewhere on this
         same toolbar. -->
